{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01175",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.62,
      "end_seconds": 5.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.63,
      "end_seconds": 14.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.96,
      "end_seconds": 21.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "So, I've been feeling tired all the time, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.14,
      "end_seconds": 25.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.89,
      "end_seconds": 28.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Probably one week. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.13,
      "end_seconds": 34.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.31,
      "end_seconds": 63.36,
      "duration_seconds": 28.05,
      "text": "Hmm, I get some relief from naps. Pretty severe, if I'm being honest. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. Uh, you know, I've also been getting out of breath on the stairs, for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 65.38,
      "end_seconds": 71.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Blood pressure 125 over 77, heart rate 116, temperature 36.5."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.65,
      "end_seconds": 74.56,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.48,
      "end_seconds": 79.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.85,
      "end_seconds": 84.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.36,
      "end_seconds": 105.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Your inner eyelids look pale and your pulse is a little fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.38,
      "end_seconds": 123.08,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.32,
      "end_seconds": 133.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Any heavy periods, black stools or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.36,
      "end_seconds": 140.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "No heavy periods, black stools or weight loss, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.48,
      "end_seconds": 145.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.34,
      "end_seconds": 147.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.58,
      "end_seconds": 153.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.89,
      "end_seconds": 156.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.76,
      "end_seconds": 180.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "So, do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.63,
      "end_seconds": 193.23,
      "duration_seconds": 11.6,
      "text": "It's rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night. Though honestly, um, some days I forget to take it. Escitalopram, 10 milligrams, maybe, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.45,
      "end_seconds": 201.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.16,
      "end_seconds": 209.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "Yeah, not with me. I'll bring it next time. I'm on a multivitamin, daily."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.66,
      "end_seconds": 216.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.83,
      "end_seconds": 219.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "For two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.2,
      "end_seconds": 223.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.25,
      "end_seconds": 234.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.75,
      "end_seconds": 237.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.14,
      "end_seconds": 241.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.87,
      "end_seconds": 244.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.9,
      "end_seconds": 249.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.52,
      "end_seconds": 254.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.7,
      "end_seconds": 271.1,
      "duration_seconds": 15.4,
      "text": "I have high cholesterol, for about ten years. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back. Ah, I've had anxiety for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.94,
      "end_seconds": 278.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "Right, so high cholesterol is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.97,
      "end_seconds": 289.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.21,
      "end_seconds": 292.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.97,
      "end_seconds": 324.58,
      "duration_seconds": 30.61,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. This is probably tiredness probably from low iron. Another possibility is low vitamin B12. I want a full blood count done, that's for tiredness. I think an iron study makes sense here, for pallor. I'd like you to take ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day, three months. It's for low iron. Take the iron with orange juice, not with tea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.72,
      "end_seconds": 353.26,
      "duration_seconds": 27.54,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Let's hold off on a thyroid test for now, and if there's no change in two weeks we can revisit it. I'd like to see you again after the results. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 354.73,
      "end_seconds": 358.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}